<title>USA: Northwestern Public Service Q1 shr falls.</title>
<headline>Northwestern Public Service Q1 shr falls.</headline>
<dateline>HURON, S.D. 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr		 $1.10		    $1.40</p>
<p> Net		 9,794		    12,508</p>
<p> Revs		284,406		  97,219</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  8,921		    8,920</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: As previously announced, the company said an accounting change resulted in higher gas costs and lower earnings in the current first quarter, but future quarters were expected to include lower gas costs and higher earnings for a neutral effect on an annual basis.</p>
<p>For the quarter ended March 31, 1996 earnings would have been $1.09 per share if the accounting change had been in effect then, the company said.</p>
<p>    -- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610 (c) Reuters Limited 1997</p>
